{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Gather yourselves and I will tell you, etc.</b> And afterward he used the language of קִבּוּץ — ״הִקָּבְצוּ וְשִׁמְעוּ״ and so forth — because our Rabbis of blessed memory said (see Pesachim 56a) that he sought to reveal the End and it was sealed off from him. Now, the term אֲסִיפָה applies to one who stands outside in an exposed place and is gathered into the house, to a private place, as in ״וַאֲסַפְתּוֹ אֶל תּוֹךְ בֵּיתֶךָ״ (Deuteronomy 22:2), ״וְאֵין אִישׁ מְאַסֵּף אוֹתִי הַבָּיְתָה״ (Judges 19:18), and so too many others. But the term קִבּוּץ indicates scattered people who gather to one place, even if it be in an exposed place where many pass through. So too: at first he sought to reveal the secret of the End, and it is not fitting to reveal a secret matter in public lest one who is unfit hear it, for ״סוֹד ה׳ לִירֵאָיו״ (Psalms 25:14) — precisely to those who fear Him. Therefore he said, ״הֵאָסְפוּ וְאַגִּידָה לָכֶם אֵת אֲשֶׁר יִקְרָא אֶתְכֶם בְּאַחֲרִית הַיָּמִים״ (Genesis 49:1), at the time of the End. And immediately he sensed in himself that the End had been sealed off from him; therefore he turned away from the language of אֲסִיפָה and said ״הִקָּבְצוּ בְּנֵי יַעֲקֹב״ (Genesis 49:2), to hear matters that contain no secret and that he could speak of in public. And he mentioned ״וְשִׁמְעוּ״ twice, because to some of them he spoke words of rebuke and reproof, such as to Reuben and Simeon and Levi, and concerning this he said ״וְשִׁמְעוּ בְנֵי יַעֲקֹב.״ And to some of them he declared future things, and concerning this he said ״וְשִׁמְעוּ אֶל יִשְׂרָאֵל אֲבִיכֶם״ (Genesis 49:2), for the telling of future things depends on the holy spirit that was upon him, which is ascribed to the name יִשְׂרָאֵל, for that name is spiritual. And this is a precious interpretation."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:34:17.801427239Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}